@Comments
.
=COMMENTS
.
.A line is a comment when its first word, after any spaces, is REM, ', ;, ##
.or //. The compiler skips the whole line.
.
:REM THE WHOLE LINE
:' THE WHOLE LINE
:; THE WHOLE LINE
:## THE WHOLE LINE
:// THE WHOLE LINE
.
.Only REM and ' can follow a statement. The comment runs to the end of the
.line.
.
:X = 1 ' THE REST OF THE LINE
:X = 1 REM THE REST OF THE LINE
.
.  - ; is a comment only at the start of a line, so PRINT A; B is a PRINT.
.  - ## is a comment and #DEFINE is not: a directive has one #.
.  - Inside a string none of these starts a comment.
.
.There is no character literal. Write ASC("A"), and the compiler folds it to
.65.
